// Sub-biome feature libraries (Phase 3.6.2).
//
// Each entry defines a feature type a Voronoi cell can carry within a
// parent biome. Placement constraints are checked against the L1
// terrain + hydrology at bake time; features that don't fit re-roll
// to another compatible feature, or fall back to a generic `plain`.
//
// Authoring notes:
// - `id`: stable string key used in the sub_biome catalog. Keep
//   snake_case.
// - `parent_biome`: which biome library this feature belongs to.
//   Must match one of the four Phase 3.6.0-pinned biomes.
// - `slope_tolerance_max_deg`: max terrain slope the feature accepts
//   at its seed position. Flat features (lakes, runways) use small
//   values; rugged features (ridges, talus) accept large slopes.
// - `roughness_tolerance_m`: max heightfield variance across a ~2 km
//   cell footprint. Low = needs flat ground (beaches, airstrips);
//   high = doesn't care (rocky ridges, forests).
// - `water_adjacency`: Required / Forbidden / None. Features needing
//   lake/river/coast presence use `Required`; features that reject
//   water (mesa top, dune field) use `Forbidden`; most use `None`.
// - `altitude_range_m`: (min, max). Cells outside this range reject.
// - `selection_weight`: relative RNG weight for selection within a
//   biome's library. Default 1.0 balances feature frequencies; tune
//   for rarity (arch_formation = 0.2 means ~5× less common than
//   baseline features).
// - `is_bleed_over_candidate`: can this feature appear in adjacent
//   biomes via the Phase 3.6.2 bleed-over mechanism? True for
//   atmospheric / water-driven features that could plausibly sneak
//   across biome lines (lake clusters, arches); False for strongly
//   biome-specific features (terracotta_port).
//
// Evolution path: add entries here over time. User flagged
// `book_cliffs` (HighDesert, Colorado-Utah region specific) as an
// initial addition beyond the MAPGEN-listed types. Pattern:
// whenever playtest or world-gen artifacts reveal a missing feel,
// author a new entry here.

(
    biomes: {
        // ── HighDesert ──────────────────────────────────────────────
        // Colorado Plateau / Grand Mesa / Colorado-Utah red-rock
        // country. User has ground-truth familiarity — see memory
        // `biome_grand_mesa_ground_truth`.
        "HighDesert": [
            (
                id: "mesa_top",
                slope_tolerance_max_deg: 3.0,
                roughness_tolerance_m: 40.0,
